### Online Canteen Food-Ordering System

### 1\. Introduction

A college canteen food-ordering system allows students to order food online without standing in long queues.

* Mobile Application: An application installed on smartphones.

* Web Application: A website accessed through a web browser.

* Progressive Web Application (PWA): A web application that provides app-like features and can be installed on a device.

### 2\. Comparison of Applications

| Feature          | Mobile App     | Web App      | PWA                       |
| ---------------- | -------------- | ------------ | ------------------------- |
| Installation     | Required       | Not required | Optional                  |
| Accessibility    | Mobile devices | Browser      | Browser and installed app |
| Notifications    | Supported      | Limited      | Supported                 |
| Offline support  | Good           | Limited      | Basic support             |
| Development cost | High           | Low          | Moderate                  |

### 3\. Suitable Application Selection

Selected: Progressive Web Application (PWA)

A PWA is the most suitable choice for the college canteen system because:

* Students can access it through a browser without downloading an app.

* It works on both mobile phones and computers.

* It supports notifications about order status.

* It is cost-effective and easy to maintain.

* It provides a fast and user-friendly experience.

### 4\. Four Major Functionalities

1\. Menu Browsing

* Displays available food items.

* Shows prices and descriptions.

* Allows students to select food items.

2\. Order Placement

* Students add food items to the cart.

* They can update quantities and confirm orders.

3\. Online Payment

* Supports online payment methods.

* Generates payment confirmation.

4\. Order Notifications

* Sends notifications when the order is accepted.

* Notifies students when food is ready for collection.

### 5\. Three Development Challenges

1\. Payment Security: Protecting students' payment details and preventing payment-related issues.

2\. Real-Time Updates: Updating order status quickly and sending notifications without delay.

3\. Network Connectivity: Ensuring the application works smoothly even with slow or unstable internet connections.

### 6\. Simple Application Workflow Diagram

### Student Opens PWA

Browse Food Menu

Select Food and Place Order

Make Online Payment

Canteen Receives Order

Prepare Food and Update Status

Student Receives Ready Notification

Collect Food

### 7\. Conclusion

A Progressive Web Application (PWA) is the best choice for the college canteen food-ordering system because it is affordable, accessible, responsive, and supports notifications. It helps students save time and reduces waiting queues in the canteen.
